1
00:00:00,367 --> 00:00:03,200
Let's look at how an OpenClaw setup works.

2
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:06,533
It's four parts, working together as one assistant.

3
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:08,900
First, OpenClaw.

4
00:00:08,900 --> 00:00:11,967
This is the software that runs your assistant.

5
00:00:11,967 --> 00:00:13,733
It receives your messages,

6
00:00:13,733 --> 00:00:16,600
works out what to do, and sends the replies.

7
00:00:17,867 --> 00:00:20,167
OpenClaw needs a computer to run on.

8
00:00:20,167 --> 00:00:24,133
That's Hostinger: a computer in the cloud that stays on day and

9
00:00:24,133 --> 00:00:28,100
night, so your assistant keeps working even when your laptop is

10
00:00:28,100 --> 00:00:28,567
closed.

11
00:00:29,833 --> 00:00:31,167
Next, the AI model.

12
00:00:31,167 --> 00:00:33,600
This is the intelligence behind it.

13
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:37,167
OpenClaw passes your request to a model like Claude,

14
00:00:37,167 --> 00:00:40,000
GPT or Gemini, which works out the answer.

15
00:00:41,267 --> 00:00:43,600
And finally, Telegram or WhatsApp.

16
00:00:43,600 --> 00:00:46,200
That's how you talk to your assistant,

17
00:00:46,200 --> 00:00:49,400
using the chat app that's already on your phone.

18
00:00:50,667 --> 00:00:51,933
Put it all together.

19
00:00:51,933 --> 00:00:55,767
You send a message, OpenClaw picks it up on its cloud computer,

20
00:00:55,767 --> 00:00:59,400
asks the AI model, and the reply comes straight back to your

21
00:00:59,400 --> 00:00:59,700
chat.
